 rts-celebrating-sima-bina\n報名/票券: https://16th-bita-prize.eventbri
 te.com\n\nJoin us for the 16th Bita Prize for Persian Arts celebrating acc
 laimed Iranian musician Sima Bina.\n\nSima Bina is a renowned Iranian folk
  singer\, songwriter\, and researcher. She is celebrated for her contribut
 ions to preserving and promoting Persian folk music and culture.\n\nSima B
 ina was born in 1945\, in Khorasan\, Iran. Her passion for folk music emer
 ged from her childhood experiences\, as she grew up surrounded by traditio
 nal Persian melodies and rhythms. She began singing at an early age and wa
 s particularly drawn to the rich tapestry of regional folk songs from diff
 erent parts of Iran.\n\nHer professional career grew in the 1960s when she
  started performing publicly and recording albums. Bina's distinctive voic
 e and her ability to interpret traditional songs with authenticity quickly
  earned her recognition within Iran and abroad.\n\nBina is also a dedicate
 d researcher and educator. Throughout her career\, Bina has tirelessly wor
 ked to collect\, document\, and preserve Persian folk music\, traveling to
  remote regions of Iran to learn from local musicians and record their son
 gs. She has amassed an extensive repertoire of folk songs representing var
 ious ethnic groups and regions of Iran\, from Kurdish lullabies to Baluchi
  melodies. She has published books on Persian folk music and has lectured 
 at universities and cultural institutions around the world\, sharing her k
 nowledge and passion for Iranian musical heritage.\n\nBina's impact on Per
 sian folk music extends beyond her own performances
